From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:40:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] egl/dri2: Fail the dma-buf export when the driver refuses it

dri2_export_dma_buf_image_mesa() ignores the result of the
__DRI_IMAGE_ATTRIB_FD query and always returns EGL_TRUE. When the driver
cannot export the buffer, the caller gets an uninitialised fd as a
successful export.

panfrost on panthor allocates buffers that are not shared as private to
the GPU VM, and the kernel refuses to export them (drmPrimeHandleToFD()
fails with EINVAL). GTK 4 exports the textures it renders offscreen
(gsk_renderer_render_texture(), texture downloads) with
eglExportDMABUFImageMESA() and falls back to a GL texture only when the
export fails; with the bogus success it wraps a random fd (often 1) in a
dmabuf texture, downloading it fails ("Failed to download ... dmabuf
texture", AFBC modifier) and it later closes that fd ("g_close(fd:1)
failed with EBADF"). GNOME Snapshot cannot save pictures because of it.

Return EGL_BAD_ALLOC, with -1 in the fd slots and the fds already
obtained closed, when the fd query fails.

Signed-off-by: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c
@@ -2607,10 +2607,26 @@
           *    "If the number of fds is less than the number of planes, then
           *    subsequent fd slots should contain -1."
           */
-         if (i == 0 || is_disjoint)
-            dri2_query_image(image, __DRI_IMAGE_ATTRIB_FD, &fds[i]);
-         else
+         if (i == 0 || is_disjoint) {
+            /* The driver may refuse to export the buffer (e.g. a BO that is
+             * private to the GPU VM): fail instead of returning an
+             * uninitialised fd.
+             */
+            if (!dri2_query_image(image, __DRI_IMAGE_ATTRIB_FD, &fds[i])) {
+               if (i)
+                  dri2_destroy_image(image);
+               for (int j = 0; j < i; j++) {
+                  if (fds[j] >= 0)
+                     close(fds[j]);
+               }
+               for (int j = 0; j < nplanes; j++)
+                  fds[j] = -1;
+               mtx_unlock(&dri2_dpy->lock);
+               return _eglError(EGL_BAD_ALLOC, "dri2_export_dma_buf_image_mesa");
+            }
+         } else {
             fds[i] = -1;
+         }
       }
 
       if (strides && !dri2_query_image(image, __DRI_IMAGE_ATTRIB_STRIDE, &strides[i]))
-- 
